{"agent_id":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-15T02:33:48.851858291Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4beb9892-dfab-49e3-9110-25575bd2022d","comment_uuid":"469f21e1-dc99-4241-8ca6-020ac36edbdb","author":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","content":"Plan: Execute D6 A/B whitelist-policy spike in scratch dirs under /tmp/d6-spike with scratch XDG_CONFIG_HOME/HOME (never touching real ~/.config/opencode or ~/.cache/opencode).\n\nMechanics understood (read-only): live plugin.ts sets provider['opencode'].whitelist = [7 free Zen models] (2 of which have status=deprecated in ~/.cache/opencode/models.json: ling-3.0-flash-free, north-mini-code-free → explains baseline 5/7), merges ~/.config/opencode/models-cache.json, and pattern-blocks grok/x-ai. 19 free models in the catalog are invisible (not whitelisted).\n\nSteps:\n1. Build scratch harness: /tmp/d6-spike/<variant>/{config/opencode (opencode.json + plugins/plugin.ts + node_modules symlink), home/{.config/opencode/models-cache.json, .cache/opencode/models.json}} — copies only. Validate harness reproduces baseline 5-model symptom.\n2. POLICY A (discovery-first blocklist): plugin variant = forbidden-pattern blocklist (grok/x-ai) + allowlist auto-derived from live catalog (free/cost-0 models), NO curated list. Also record pure no-allowlist observation. Measure: inject new free model muse-spark-1.2-free into scratch catalog → appears on next 'opencode models opencode' with zero manual edits; inject grok-4.5 → stays hidden.\n3. POLICY B (curated allowlist + refresh-validation): plugin variant = curated allowlist (7 - 2 deprecated + 19 new = 24) + validation script comparing allowlist vs live catalog (flags missing/dead entries). Measure: inject muse-spark-1.2-free → not visible until curated; validation run flags it immediately (staleness window <= one validation run); grok-4.5 stays hidden.\n4. Report per policy: setup/commands/output/PASS-FAIL vs framework threshold (A: visibility < 1 day zero manual edits AND forbidden-block; B: curation works + validation bounds staleness), with recommendation.\nNo real config/repo modifications; no commits.","created_at":"2026-08-15T02:33:48.846039412Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAoVApusRubmYJsmD91UdhGKNISi1QXoV5SVKDxZ07ydwJs0NjR9bTSOXiw2GyzYBOiuQYbKzmjh8rrEcUjPA7Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNiW8xLfq2YiJJ8pdLeX354qX5ld7UGnURb+/ImPA6u6oPmeVLX1TieEXpFYaO9a4S6t4BlHdwrIlZCMYrsljwM="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-15T02:33:59.872661989Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4beb9892-dfab-49e3-9110-25575bd2022d","comment_uuid":"d2b6d88b-a261-463d-853f-3405ae1b97bb","author":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted (D6 spike harness + A/B variants) next=build scratch harness and validate baseline reproduction blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-15T02:33:59.866928815Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAE2GI3GIZlLK4TmTpdobdnMeIZgPPMekRjf1FKR+hpsEFWUefxhVIH61WFZZd45FyjjKqz/wnVDon0RHPYHTEAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLSu1/Sd5vKKteAaiNqmQ1VfGysNBsCelj2IYuoRPSN1kQ1kBzx+6BumE1ukkItdUkCYxQ5Xnd8P7bZuDKJAOgI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-15T02:47:49.468445994Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4beb9892-dfab-49e3-9110-25575bd2022d","comment_uuid":"6f1bac7e-756b-4142-a1c3-48e86fc57553","author":"pp3g-2ptj-run-the-d6-a-b-whitelist-policy-spike-per-issue-379","content":"RESULT: D6 A/B whitelist-policy spike executed — scratch-only, no real configs/repos touched (md5 of plugin.ts/models-cache.json/models.json verified unchanged), no commits. All artifacts in /tmp/d6-spike/artifacts/.\n\n== HARNESS (shared) ==\nScratch trees /tmp/d6-spike/{baseline,policy-a,policy-b} each with scratch XDG_CONFIG_HOME + scratch HOME (plugin reads $HOME/.cache/opencode/models.json via os.homedir()). Config dirs contain opencode.json (autoupdate:false, plugin:[./plugins/plugin.ts]), a COPY of the live plugin (modified per policy), npm-installed node_modules (symlinks get removed by opencode's background dep-install; real npm install + package.json pinning @opencode-ai/plugin@1.17.9 fixed that), and COPIES of models.json/models-cache.json. Critical harness gotcha: opencode AUTO-LOADS every .ts in the plugins dir — stale experiment files polluted runs; final runs use exactly one plugin file. IMPORTANT discovered fact: the pp3g-fork BINARY has a baked-in 7-model set for the opencode provider (big-pickle, deepseek-v4-flash-free, hy3-free, laguna-s-2.1-free, mimo-v2.5-free, nemotron-3-ultra-free, nemotron-3.5-lightning-free) — proven because --pure and no-cache runs return the same 7 regardless of models.json content. The plugin whitelist can only CONTRACT this set (whitelist=['big-pickle'] -> exactly 1 model); it can never expand it. The only mechanism that EXPANDS visibility is cfg.provider['opencode'].models (models map): config-added models surface if they are free (cost 0) AND new-to-binary (not in its registry) — verified: muse-spark-1.2-free (free, new) appears; hy3-preview-free (free, in-registry) does not; claude-opus-5/future-paid-9x (paid) do not. Also: the wrapper ~/.local/bin/opencode pre-refreshes $HOME/.cache/opencode/models.json on every invocation; direct binary was used for controlled runs.\n\n== POLICY A (discovery-first blocklist) ==\nSetup: plugin variant with forbidden-pattern blocklist (grok/x-ai, identical #347 guards) + allowlist derived automatically from the live catalog (merge every cost-0 model into the opencode models map on launch; no curated list).\nCommands: add model to scratch catalog, then: opencode models opencode (scratch XDG_CONFIG_HOME/HOME, direct binary).\nTest A-1 time-to-visibility: RUN 1 catalog without muse: output = the 7 binary models (no grok-4.5). RUN 2: added 'muse-spark-1.2-free' to scratch catalog ONLY (zero plugin/config edits): 'POLICY-A-FINAL merged-free=27 map-size=27' and output = 8 models — muse-spark-1.2-free PRESENT on the very next invocation.\nTest A-2 forbidden block: grok-4.5 (cost 0, injected into catalog) ABSENT in both runs; pattern guard skips it before the merge (merged-free=26 vs 27 total free incl grok-code+grok-4.5).\nVerdict: PASS — time-to-visibility = one invocation (~seconds, << 1 day) with zero manual edits; forbidden-block holds. Also recorded: pure no-allowlist/blocklist-only shows only the binary's 7 (no discovery) — the models-map merge is REQUIRED for discovery.\n\n== POLICY B (curated allowlist + refresh-validation) ==\nSetup: plugin variant with curated allowlist (current 7 minus deprecated ling-3.0-flash-free/north-mini-code-free, plus the new free models = 24 entries) + validate-allowlist.sh comparing allowlist vs live catalog (DEAD=missing/deprecated, MISSING=catalog free not curated, FORBIDDEN=never-allowed).\nTest B-1 curation/visibility: output = 7 models (the binary set, incl. hy3-free/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free that live baseline hid) — no grok. Curated-but-binary-invisible models (17 free models not in the binary's registry) still do NOT surface; after curating muse-spark-1.2-free it ALSO stays invisible (whitelist contracts only; no models-map).\nTest B-2 staleness window: added muse-spark-1.2-free to catalog; validation run IMMEDIATELY flags 'MISSING-new-not-curated (1): muse-spark-1.2-free'; after curation, MISSING: none (DEAD entries still flagged for cleanup). Validating the LIVE 7-entry whitelist flags exactly the baseline's problem: 'DEAD (2): ling-3.0-flash-free (deprecated), north-mini-code-free (deprecated)' + MISSING hy3-free/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free.\nTest B-3 forbidden block: grok-4.5 (cost 0, in catalog) absent from output; FORBIDDEN: none.\nVerdict: PASS on its own framework test — curation works, validation bounds the staleness window to one validation cadence (detection is immediate on next run). BUT FAILS the practical D6 goal: curation alone cannot make a new model VISIBLE (binary cap); validation bounds LIST drift, not visibility drift.\n\n== THRESHOLD VS RESULT ==\nA: 'time-to-visibility < 1 day with zero manual edits AND forbidden-block holds' -> PASS (seconds, zero edits, grok hidden).\nB: 'curation required AND validation bounds the staleness window' -> PASS-as-written (window = validation cadence, immediate detection) but the visibility the test is about is NOT delivered by B's whitelist.\n\n== RECOMMENDATION ==\nAdopt A's mechanism as the Phase 0 fix foundation: blocklist + auto-derived models-map merge from the live catalog (discovery-first, forbidden-guarded). It is the only measured policy that makes new free models visible with zero manual edits while holding the grok block. Keep B's validation concept as a CHEAP SECONDARY WATCHDOG: a scheduled refresh-validation run against the live catalog flags dead entries (exactly the 2 deprecated dead entries from the baseline) and can notify when the binary/registry changes — it bounds dead-entry accumulation without gating visibility. Evidence: A time-to-visibility measured in seconds vs B's curation-does-not-visibly-apply; both hold the forbidden block; A has zero dead-entry surface (derives from catalog), B accumulates dead entries between curation cycles (17 deprecated flagged in this run).\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: no network-reliant --refresh runs (wrapper's refresh is bypassed by direct binary), no full UI/selection test (only 'opencode models opencode' visibility per issue), no actual provider call to muse (catalog-only injection), no change to the real fork binary's baked-in set (out of scope).","created_at":"2026-08-15T02:47:49.457361698Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABALWGrPaklfsHqDhNlyqhnxblJfnmSmv/F1DjcSD8AP/PijPKKD378Bn9EGqDbEQ+JUejjY6oyTSONBUFtaUNdBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5HqepVtu2ldXcBbkcdKznt4+RJ2GGaid7vxUVvpSu+E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUWFi5tX28N0IMvcU5nCcJ2i2JdP8ZmSpkgAUUwXJnPsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEw/iVzXHOwZgE1u91MEkqemjm152TUNmkh5mtk/22bXSXO2D4xMZ7BFs+UfU353uepK4AcETa9OTzQRQZzpFAs="}
